{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Hear, I pray, this dream.</b> The reason he said ״na״ is as I explained, that they did not want to hear; he therefore said to them ״na״ in the language of a request." "<b>Or</b> it may intend along the lines of what they said, of blessed memory (Berakhot 56a), that the essential fulfillment of a dream is specifically on its day and not on another day, and therefore one fasts the fast of a dream even on Shabbat and it is not postponed to another day. For this reason he said <b>na</b>, meaning, now, and do not delay it to another time, so that it may be fulfilled. Furthermore, he intended to tell them lest they think that he had already gone to those who show him kindness and his friends and told them the dream, and they interpreted it for good — and if so, the good plan he intended, to draw the hearts of his brothers closer, as I explained in the preceding verse, would be void, for there would be no proof that they are in the presumption of loving friends, since the essential interpretation had already preceded and they had interpreted it for good. As a sign of this, he did not bother coming to them, for even if they interpreted it for evil, the first interpretation had already been fulfilled; therefore he said ״na.״ And if you say: but did they not say in the chapter HaRo'eh (Berakhot 55b)? Rabbi Bena'ah said: once I dreamed a single dream and went to twenty-four dream-interpreters who were in Jerusalem, and what one interpreted for me another did not interpret for me, and all of them were fulfilled in me — end quote. Perhaps that is specifically when the interpretations do not contradict one another, but if they contradict, a second interpreter cannot override the first interpretation. And Joseph was concerned that they might suspect him of this, so he said <b>hear, I pray</b>, meaning, now he is relating the matter, and he had not previously related it to anyone else." "<b>This dream.</b> He said the letter heh of definiteness, because he had already told them that he had dreamed a dream without specifying the dream, and then returned to say: Hear, I pray, this dream that I told you I dreamed."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:46:25.883189816Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}